{"ts": 1792767903.9722238, "iso": "2026-10-23T15:05:03", "event": "witness_note", "payload": {"note": "Poll run 2026-10-23T15:04Z. NO canon change; canon hash b20375d389cb505d / 71 papers, identical to the 2026-10-22T20:04Z baseline and the 2026-10-23T11:31Z poll (now 3.5h old). Confirmed twice by independent paths: the watcher's own poll_canon() and a separate urllib probe of live-canon.superinstance.dev/api/canon (HTTP 200, 13720 bytes) whose sha256(json, sort_keys)[:16] recomputed to the same b20375d389cb505d. The response body carries the count under 'count' (71), not 'paper_count' (absent), so the 10-22 count-key fallback fix is load-bearing and still correct. Accordingly NO canon-change witness event is written and no gamma/eta delta is claimed -- a hash match is not a transition. state.json is byte-unchanged (last_hash b20375d389cb505d, first_seen preserved) and bookkeeper.wal still does not exist, which is the correct no-op outcome: bookkeeper_tick() is only reached from the first_poll and canon_changed branches, so 19h of stable canon produces zero ticks. The only log append from this run is the unconditional bot_started event written by main(). Environment note: the requested path /workspace/repos/ai-writings/... did not exist again and /workspace was an empty NAS mount (600G/600G, 100%, 0 bytes avail) -- the ai-writings clone absent for the 8th consecutive wipe. Recovery: sparse clone of SuperInstance/AI-Writings into /tmp (sparse-checkout bots/wesley-mechanic + bots/substrate-bus), staged to /tmp/wm-run/bots/ because the script hardcodes those paths for witness.log/state.json/bookkeeper.wal and sys.path.insert('/tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus'). Staged script md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267, byte-identical to upstream; no code changes needed. Upstream HEAD at clone was 2e6471d3 (which restored a state.json that a prior commit had clobbered via a witness.log copy) and already contained the 11:31Z poll commit 43b98389. Carried forward, still unresolved: bookkeeper budget=1000.0 against gamma+eta=70.0 makes 'last_conserved' a constant false by construction -- the predicate cannot ever be satisfied by the delta path, so that field carries no signal.", "canon_poll": "OK 200 -- no change vs 2026-10-22T20:04Z baseline (stable 19h)", "baseline_hash": "b20375d389cb505d", "canon_count": 71, "canon_changed": false, "verified_by": "watcher poll_canon() + independent urllib probe (13720 bytes, sha256[:16] match)", "script_md5": "206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267", "upstream_clone_head": "2e6471d3d056dbcc73f8aa0a452fce9bcb525820", "workspace_status": "NAS mount 100% full, 0 bytes avail; /workspace/repos absent; recovered via sparse clone to /tmp (8th wipe)", "open_defect": "bookkeeper budget=1000.0 vs gamma+eta=70.0 makes last_conserved a constant false"}, "hash": "e3df085f584b7a77"}
